    <ferc:NumberOfBarrelMilesOnTrunkLinesOfOilProducts id="f-885" contextRef="c-17" unitRef="u-06" decimals="0">4664518659</ferc:NumberOfBarrelMilesOnTrunkLinesOfOilProducts>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-887" contextRef="c-17">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE A - ORGANIZATION, OPERATIONS AND BASIS OF PRESENTATION:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Organization.&lt;/b&gt; Orbit Gulf Coast NGL Exports, LLC (&amp;quot;Orbit&amp;quot;) is a Delaware limited liability company. Energy Transfer Nederland Terminal, LLC (&amp;quot;ETNT&amp;quot;), a wholly owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer LP, owns 58.1% interest in Orbit. Satellite Chemical USA Corp. owns a 41.9% interest in Orbit.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Operations&lt;/b&gt;. Orbit owns and operates an ethane pipeline system with a throughput capacity of approximately 182 thousand barrels per day (&amp;quot;MBbls/d&amp;quot;), delivering from Energy Transfer Mont Belvieu NGL's Texas storage and fractionation complex to our marine terminal in Nederland, Texas, as well as a 182 MBbls/d ethane refrigeration facility and 1.32 million standard barrels (&amp;quot;MMBbls&amp;quot;) of storage capacity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Regulation.&lt;/b&gt; Orbit's natural gas liquids (&amp;quot;NGL&amp;quot;) transportation activities are subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;quot;FERC&amp;quot;) and various state authorities. Regulatory bodies exercise statutory authority over matters such as rates, underlying accounting practices, and rate-making agreements with customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Basis of Presentation.&lt;/b&gt; The financial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which constitute a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (&amp;quot;GAAP&amp;quot;). The most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income and statement of cash flows and (2) use of FERC approved depreciation rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE B - SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES AND OTHER MATTERS:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The preparation of financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and the reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reporting period. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Cash equivalents consist of highly liquid investments, which are readily convertible into cash and have original maturities of three months or less. The cash deposits and temporary cash investments are placed with high credit quality financial institutions. At times, Orbit's cash and cash equivalents may be uninsured or in deposit accounts that exceed the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation insurance limit.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Property, Plant and Equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Orbit capitalizes expenditures related to property, plant and equipment that have a useful life greater than one year for (1) assets purchased or constructed; (2) existing assets that are replaced or improved; or (3) land regardless of cost. During construction, Orbit capitalizes direct costs, such as labor, materials, and other costs, such as interest during construction, overhead and security costs. Orbit records property, plant and equipment at its original cost. Depreciation is computed on a composite straight-line method at the FERC authorized rates based on the expected economic lives of the various classes of assets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Accounts Receivable and Allowance for Credit Losses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Accounts receivable are carried at the amount owed by customers less an allowance for credit losses, if deemed necessary. Orbit evaluates the collectability of accounts receivable based on review of a specific customer's ability to meet its financial obligation or as a result of changes in the overall aging of accounts receivable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Orbit's allowance for credit losses was not material as of December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Contract Balances with Customers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Orbit satisfies its obligations by transferring goods or services in exchange for consideration from customers. The timing of performance may differ from the timing that the associated consideration is received from the customer, thus resulting in the recognition of a contract liability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Orbit recognizes a contract liability if the customer's payment of consideration precedes Orbit's fulfillment of the performance obligations. Certain contracts contain provisions requiring customers to pay a fixed fee for a right to use the Orbit's assets, but allow customers to apply such fees against services to be provided at a future point in time. These amounts are reflected as deferred revenue until the customer applies the deficiency fees to services provided or becomes unable to use the fees as payment for future services due to expiration of the contractual period the fees can be applied or physical inability of the customer to utilize the fees due to capacity constraints. As of December 31, 2025, no contract liabilities have been recognized. For the year ended December 31, 2024, contract liabilities of $11.4 million were recognized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Obligations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;At contract inception, Orbit assesses the goods and services promised in its contracts with customers and identifies a performance obligation for each promise to transfer a good or service that is distinct. Revenue is recognized when (or as) the performance obligations are satisfied, that is, when the customer obtains control of the good or service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Orbit generally does not own the NGL that it transports or stores.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Orbit is a limited liability company that has elected to be treated as a partnership for income tax purposes. Accordingly, no provision for federal income taxes has been recorded in the financial statements of Orbit, and the tax effects of Orbit's activities generally accrue to the members. However, Orbit is subject to gross margins tax enacted by the State of Texas, and therefore has recorded state income taxes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Environmental Remediation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Orbit accrues environmental remediation costs for work at identified sites where an assessment has indicated that cleanup costs are probable and reasonably estimable. Such accruals are undiscounted and are based on currently available information, estimated timing of remedial actions and related inflation assumptions, existing technology and presently enacted laws and regulations. If a range of probable environmental cleanup costs exists for an identified site, the minimum of the range is accrued unless some other point or points in the range are more likely, in which case the most likely amount in this range is accrued. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, there were no amounts accrued for future environmental expenditures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE C - COMMITMENTS AND CONTINGENCIES:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Orbit may be subject to various legal proceedings and claims that arise in the ordinary course of business. In the opinion of management, the amount of any ultimate liability with respect to any such actions will not materially affect Orbit's financial position or results of operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE D - RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Operating Management Fees&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Orbit pays ETNT an annual fixed operating fee of approximately $1.0 million per year as reimbursement for providing certain services including business development, legal services, accounting and financial reporting, human resource services, and other as defined in the operating agreement. The fixed operating fee is escalated annually by one percent and is ETNT's sole reimbursement and compensation for any allocation of ETNT's or its affiliates' overhead related to the services.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The fixed operating fee amounted to $1.0 million for each of the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE E - SUPPLEMENTAL CASH FLOW INFORMATION:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Accrued capital expenditures as of December 31, 2025 and 2024 were $1.9 million and nil, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
