        <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="f-131_lbl" order="0" xlink:to="ft-131_47270_lbl" />
        <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="f-907_lbl" order="0" xlink:to="ft-907_47402_lbl" />
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-131_47270_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">The following are the intermediary companies in the chain of ownership between Energy Transfer LP (DE) and Orbit Gulf Coast NGL Exports, LLC (DE):</span></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Energy Transfer LP indirectly through affiliates owns 100% of Energy Transfer Nederland Terminal (TX) via the following chain of ownership:</span></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Energy Transfer LP owns 100% interests in  Energy Transfer Nederland Terminal through its 100% ownership of ET COAM Holdings LLC (DE). Energy Transfer Nederland Terminal owns 58.1% of Orbit Gulf Coast NGL Exports, LLC.</span></span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-907_47402_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b style="font-weight: bold; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-style: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)">Schedule Page 700 Line No.: 9 Column: b</b></span></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">The cost of service results were calculated using the Cost of Service Model. This model calculates cost of service using the Trended Original Cost methodology promulgated by the FERC in Opinion No. 154-B, 31 FERC  61,377 (1985), as modified and clarified by subsequent rulings.</span></span></p></div></link:footnote>
    </link:footnoteLink>
</xbrl>